{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## Closing verdict — all 9 ACs adjudicated against the LANDED tree\n\nLanded as Gerrit change **3163**, patch set 2 = `e096a33d3b7` (`current_revision`),\n`Change-Id I340d8e74ed9aa92e6259ac9dfbe4d434b6f15d44`, status MERGED with\n**`LLM-Review +1`** and **`Verified +1`**, submitted 2026-10-31.\n\n- **AC1 — PASS.** The retirement grep over `src` returns empty on the landed tree.\n- **AC2 — PASS.** The second grep returns empty.\n- **AC3, AC4, AC6, AC7, AC9 — PASS on the `Verified +1`.** Each names a subset of what\n  CI's gating `ubuntu-latest, py3.13` cell runs; that cell runs `make verify`, a strict\n  superset, and it voted green on the merged revision.\n- **AC5 — PASS.** The golden surface census carries the expected row at\n  `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py:170`.\n\n- **AC8 — NOT MET AS WRITTEN; recorded as a defect in the plan, not in the work.**\n  AC8 asserts the change touches exactly **5** paths. The landed diff touches **6**. The\n  sixth is `docs/env-vars.md`, and it is not optional: `make lint` runs\n  `scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check`, which fails unless that file is regenerated\n  whenever the env surface moves. So AC8 and **AC9** (`make verify` green) could not both\n  be satisfied — satisfying AC8's count would have failed AC9, and the change correctly\n  chose AC9.\n\n  The error is in AC8's arithmetic at authoring time: the plan enumerated the source and\n  test paths and omitted the generated doc its own approach compels. No work is missing and\n  no extra work was done; the sixth path is the mechanical consequence of the five.\n\n  Closing on substance per the operator decision of this session. The generalisable lesson —\n  an AC that pins an exact file count must include every artifact a `--check` generator\n  compels — is the same class as bug `6f24-3d47-b251-4905` (an AC asserting a condition the\n  tooling cannot produce) and is filed alongside the other plan-authoring amendments."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793445091151470001,"uuid":"d6bdd783-2dbf-4275-9dbf-3243e733e6bf"}